                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1a16432-c3bc-362f-8275-a7d65a82bee0",
                        "entry_id": "b75044e6-8009-30aa-a290-0f3a8821bea0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who sculls; an athlete who participates in sculling races."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c4defee-361e-456b-a6e1-b46e026da4f9",
                                "sense_id": "d1a16432-c3bc-362f-8275-a7d65a82bee0",
                                "text": "[…] each man discharged their péece, and killed the sayd waterman, which forthwith falling downe dead, the Sculler with much payne rowed through the Bridge to the Tower wharffe with the Lieutenants man, and the dead man in his boate […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f97294b-e382-4f9e-983d-19671f5711b9",
                                "sense_id": "d1a16432-c3bc-362f-8275-a7d65a82bee0",
                                "text": "The first and second guns had been fired, and the scullers in their boats, each some ten yards apart from the other, are anxiously waiting the firing of the third, which is the signal for starting."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2977bd92-447f-3c8b-87e2-c49624593a17",
                        "entry_id": "b75044e6-8009-30aa-a290-0f3a8821bea0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A boat rowed by one person with two sculls, or short oars."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "113c338a-07c5-4cab-9dce-dbb279f1a743",
                                "sense_id": "2977bd92-447f-3c8b-87e2-c49624593a17",
                                "text": "1675, John Dryden, The Mistaken Husband, London: J. Magnes and R. Bentley, Act III, p. 33,\nAlas! the Story's short: Your Father’s dead. He would needs take water in a Sculler; And to save part of the Charges, going to row, overturned the Boat upon a Buoy […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33d9ca0f-6c83-43ab-b7c7-f028c650ec5d",
                                "sense_id": "2977bd92-447f-3c8b-87e2-c49624593a17",
                                "text": "The Boats being clear, the Captain’s Boat, which was Oars, and consequently had two Watermen, went before the Maid’s Boat, which was but a Sculler; and as he passed by, looking at the Wench, he thought he knew her Face, but did not call to mind who she was […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14fd21c1-8282-4620-8116-d3720456b60b",
                                "sense_id": "2977bd92-447f-3c8b-87e2-c49624593a17",
                                "text": "At that time, the steam-traffic on the Thames was far below its present extent, and watermen’s boats were far more numerous. […] Early as it was, there were plenty of scullers going here and there that morning, and plenty of barges dropping down with the tide […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5ebae33-9db6-4e56-9951-38e3be2fb14c",
                                "sense_id": "2977bd92-447f-3c8b-87e2-c49624593a17",
                                "text": "They watched that boat. It was a double sculler, with two female figures in the stern; it came slothfully up past the ferry; the sculling was not very good […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3544231-df34-4550-b756-00725dd75971",
                        "source_entry_id": "b75044e6-8009-30aa-a290-0f3a8821bea0",
                        "source_sense_description": "one who sculls",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ruderer",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ruderer",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7cb72b5-e30a-3219-9298-f99868cafb6a",
                                        "entry_id": "f62180b1-ae08-34a6-abca-4f8b819bd5f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Person, die ein Boot rudert"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd013090-ccdf-4302-9384-cf06d37b95e6",
                                                "sense_id": "f7cb72b5-e30a-3219-9298-f99868cafb6a",
                                                "text": "„Auf die gleiche Weise werden die Sitzbalken für die Ruderer eingezogen und fixiert.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f7ffacd-d77c-4888-8d1c-ed30d5b48c1d",
                                                "sense_id": "f7cb72b5-e30a-3219-9298-f99868cafb6a",
                                                "text": "„Die Ruderer schafften stromabwärts vier Meilen pro Stunde und stromaufwärts die Hälfte.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3a182af-baee-4221-b5e7-2b736a2ef4ce",
                                                "sense_id": "f7cb72b5-e30a-3219-9298-f99868cafb6a",
                                                "text": "„Ich verließ Korfu bei Einbruch der Nacht und kam am frühen Morgen in Otranto an, ohne daß meine Ruderer auch nur einmal ihre Ruder eintauchten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d2ed0e2-b499-46b0-97f0-8f8683174505",
                                                "sense_id": "f7cb72b5-e30a-3219-9298-f99868cafb6a",
                                                "text": "„Sein Offizier wandte sich nun zu den Ruderern, die noch im Boote saßen, und erteilte ihnen die ihm zugekommenen Orders.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
